<section class="content-card">

<h2>CGPA calculation formula</h2>

<div class="formula">
<strong>CGPA =</strong>
Total Quality Points ÷ Total Credit Hours
</div>

<p>
For each semester, multiply the semester GPA by its credit hours.
Then add all quality points and divide them by the total credit hours.
</p>

</section>

<section class="content-card">

<h2>Example</h2>

<div class="example">

Semester 1: GPA 3.50 × 15 credits = 52.50
<br>

Semester 2: GPA 3.70 × 15 credits = 55.50
<br><br>

Total Quality Points = 108.00
<br>
Total Credit Hours = 30
<br><br>

<strong>CGPA = 108 ÷ 30 = 3.60</strong>

</div>

